meta {
  name: Confirm payment
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/orders/:id/confirm-payment
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  id: 1
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{staffToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "method": "bank-transfer",
    "reference": "TT-1"
  }
}

docs {
  Staff, with `orders.manage`. This is the step that turns a pro forma into a commercial
  invoice, and it exists because somebody has to look at a bank statement.

  The pro forma is left exactly as it was — the buyer holds a copy, and a document that changed
  after they were given it is not a record of anything.

  A second confirmation is **409**, not a second invoice. Cancelling a paid order is also 409:
  that is a refund, and it has its own route.
}
